content:
Excited to see this paper out from the excellent 
@JulianDJacobs
, part of our economics group at 
@GoogleDeepMind
, and Jordan Canedy. 

They look at the impact of prior worker retraining programs, finding that contrary to their purpose, most workers stay in the same or similarly exposed sector after retraining.

This is the first paper from our group. Much more to come!

@sebkrier wrote:
> The main federally-funded worker retraining program in the US (WIOA) rarely shifts workers out of automation-vulnerable work: 45% of participants return to their prior industry and 27% stay in the same occupation. 

The authors use RTI (how routine/automatable a job's tasks are),

Relatable.

